  "description": "Works to tree with a TCA: T001 - Common Ash (Fraxinus excelsior), located within the rear garden of 6 Dulwich Common, London, SE21 7EX, as identified on the accompanying tree location plan.\r\rProposed works: Fell the tree to ground level.\r\rThe tree is approximately 15 metres in height, with a stem diameter of 400 mm. It has been classified as Category U in accordance with BS5837:2012, with an estimated remaining life expectancy of less than 10 years.\r\rThe arboricultural survey identified dead branches in the lower canopy, deadwood and canopy dieback, together with dead foliage indicating the presence of ash dieback.\r\rThe proposed removal is supported by the arboricultural findings regarding the tree's deteriorating condition and limited remaining life expectancy.\r\rAll tree works will be undertaken by a suitably qualified and insured tree contractor.\r\rReplacement planting will be undertaken in accordance with the Dulwich Estate approval conditions.",
